*************************************** Raw Data Analysis (Data Discovery)
- Quick Data Discovery step (Snowflake, CSV, etc)
Entities: What real-world "things" are in this data?
    Example: Parts, Customers, Orders.
Relationships: How do these "things" connect to each other?
    Example: "Customer A placed Order #101 for Engine Part X."
Data Quality & Fixes: Is anything messy or confusing?
    Timezones: Are dates in UTC, PST, or local time? We must standardize them so Tony sees accurate sales dates.
    Formatting: Are text values uppercase in some rows and lowercase in others?
    Missing/Null values: Are there orders without customer IDs?
Normalisation: Is information split cleanly into tables, or is it all dumped into one giant, messy spreadsheet?


